// EXPECT-DIAG: E004
// EXPECT-DIAG: Cannot initialize an array of 'int' with a value of type 'string'
// Regression test: an array declaration's initializer list elements must
// match the declared element type. Before this fix, TypeChecker::
// visitArrayDecl() visited each initializer (so each got its own inferred
// type) but never compared that type against the declared element type --
// unlike the sibling ArrayLiteralExprAST path (visitArrayLiteral), which
// DOES cross-check its elements. Confirmed as a genuine type-safety hole,
// not just a missing diagnostic: `int[3] arr = [1, "two", 3]` compiled with
// zero diagnostic, and reading `arr[1] to string` back printed the string
// literal's raw pointer bits reinterpreted as an int.

fn main(): int {
    mut arr: int[3] = [1, "two", 3];
    return 0;
}
